  "body": "As mentioned in https://github.com/WICG/webusb/issues/217 it would be safe and useful for methods accepting an `BufferSource` to instead accept an `AllowSharedBufferSource`.\r\n\r\nThe argument for safety is that because the `ArrayBuffer` is already not transferred it is possible for script to modify its contents before the data is sent to the device, allowing this modification to come from another thread is roughly a no-op. In the Chromium implementation in particular, the buffer contents is immediately copied into an IPC message anyways and so the window of opportunity for modification is quite short.",
